1856" :step/content "question-745d6485-4fab-5db3-ad5a-442675f1d8d6" :step/next "step-24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :step/id #uuid "24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :step/content "question-1ac9a15a-91b5-5333-bd21-1c4aeb66e1dd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064281 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/id #uuid "bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48637" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ at the point where $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" "answer-9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" "answer-4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" "answer-527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/id #uuid "16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" :answer/id #uuid "9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" :answer/id #uuid "4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" :answer/id #uuid "527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer/id #uuid "9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064282 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/id #uuid "c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-48639" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, we find \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =-4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" "answer-17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" "answer-99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" "answer-a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/id #uuid "f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer/id #uuid "8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" :answer/id #uuid "17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" :answer/id #uuid "99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af" :answer/id #uuid "a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064283 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/id #uuid "6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72159" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=3{cos}^{2}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=3{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=6u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =6u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/id #uuid "6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" "answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" "answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" "answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/id #uuid "9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/id #uuid "41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/id #uuid "b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/id #uuid "5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/id #uuid "ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065335 :tutorial/content "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064405 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198279 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1aeeb90-b252-58b0-bd1f-5b12f471387e" "question-260f8856-8d02-57c2-89b0-9f4ad3929290" "question-b91cf75b-843d-5d15-ac06-6485f918c5af" "question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1aeeb90-b252-58b0-bd1f-5b12f471387e" :question/id #uuid "b1aeeb90-b252-58b0-bd1f-5b12f471387e" :question/math-academy-id "q-175364" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}-8=2x$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}-8=2x$\n\nNow, we solve the above equation by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8 & =2x \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-2\\in R$ and $x=4\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=\\{-2,4\\}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf86a146-26ce-5ad8-bf9e-055735de44f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf86a146-26ce-5ad8-bf9e-055735de44f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf86a146-26ce-5ad8-bf9e-055735de44f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74b55427-77a5-5628-b490-8b51f45c46ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74b55427-77a5-5628-b490-8b51f45c46ac" "answer-4c9a04ac-26ec-5ead-8bb8-50236f13de94" "answer-2e5e32b3-c4e2-5b66-8f6f-22792540ff8d" "answer-aa928a83-e518-5b7c-90af-6f77aa25fe2a" "answer-a8dddfc1-8b64-58af-9ae6-c3ee7f6700d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74b55427-77a5-5628-b490-8b51f45c46ac" :answer/id #uuid "74b55427-77a5-5628-b490-8b51f45c46ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c9a04ac-26ec-5ead-8bb8-50236f13de94" :answer/id #uuid "4c9a04ac-26ec-5ead-8bb8-50236f13de94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-4,-2,2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e5e32b3-c4e2-5b66-8f6f-22792540ff8d" :answer/id #uuid "2e5e32b3-c4e2-5b66-8f6f-22792540ff8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-4,-2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa928a83-e518-5b7c-90af-6f77aa25fe2a" :answer/id #uuid "aa928a83-e518-5b7c-90af-6f77aa25fe2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8dddfc1-8b64-58af-9ae6-c3ee7f6700d2" :answer/id #uuid "a8dddfc1-8b64-58af-9ae6-c3ee7f6700d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-260f8856-8d02-57c2-89b0-9f4ad3929290" :question/id #uuid "260f8856-8d02-57c2-89b0-9f4ad3929290" :question/math-academy-id "q-175353" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is divisible by $3,$\n\nwhere the universal set is the set of integers from $5$ to $20$ inclusive." :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* $T$ of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is\n\n$$\nU=\\{5,6,…,20\\}.\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nThe following numbers give the elements of our truth set:\n\n- $x=6$ since $6$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=9$ since $9$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=12$ since $12$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=15$ since $15$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=18$ since $18$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=\\{6,9,12,15,18\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cfa5d698-eb34-58cf-9780-238b5cb9eb58"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cfa5d698-eb34-58cf-9780-238b5cb9eb58" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfa5d698-eb34-58cf-9780-238b5cb9eb58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1ef07448-0b15-5f77-831a-c55328b61392" :answer-field/choices ["answer-342225e3-b744-59a4-a18e-552c1ed57177" "answer-c4b0a66d-4234-5ffe-8314-ca3a322857d3" "answer-1ef07448-0b15-5f77-831a-c55328b61392" "answer-c02e9e86-772c-50d4-8c6d-4c63a835a6f4" "answer-0b59d398-5c35-51d7-a940-fbf48c21c719"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-342225e3-b744-59a4-a18e-552c1ed57177" :answer/id #uuid "342225e3-b744-59a4-a18e-552c1ed57177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,10,12,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4b0a66d-4234-5ffe-8314-ca3a322857d3" :answer/id #uuid "c4b0a66d-4234-5ffe-8314-ca3a322857d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,9,10,13,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ef07448-0b15-5f77-831a-c55328b61392" :answer/id #uuid "1ef07448-0b15-5f77-831a-c55328b61392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,9,12,15,18\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c02e9e86-772c-50d4-8c6d-4c63a835a6f4" :answer/id #uuid "c02e9e86-772c-50d4-8c6d-4c63a835a6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,9,12,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b59d398-5c35-51d7-a940-fbf48c21c719" :answer/id #uuid "0b59d398-5c35-51d7-a940-fbf48c21c719" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,9,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b91cf75b-843d-5d15-ac06-6485f918c5af" :question/id #uuid "b91cf75b-843d-5d15-ac06-6485f918c5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-175358" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $4x-3\\ge 9,$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $4x-3\\ge 9$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nNow, we need to solve the above inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3\\ge 9 \\\\ 4x\\ge 12 \\\\ x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=[3,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20ae3d0b-c166-52e0-b469-1972d9f84ee6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20ae3d0b-c166-52e0-b469-1972d9f84ee6" :answer-field/id #uuid "20ae3d0b-c166-52e0-b469-1972d9f84ee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e526436b-9a51-5f65-a668-0eb96ca49eb0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ceb9044e-2366-52a5-89ec-803aba63111e" "answer-0b68889d-10d4-51c4-be9b-87b0c97af70e" "answer-6189dc4e-a81c-5882-83eb-6da2f69c3dcc" "answer-bace1e39-b96c-5598-91da-f2e30385e626" "answer-e526436b-9a51-5f65-a668-0eb96ca49eb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceb9044e-2366-52a5-89ec-803aba63111e" :answer/id #uuid "ceb9044e-2366-52a5-89ec-803aba63111e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b68889d-10d4-51c4-be9b-87b0c97af70e" :answer/id #uuid "0b68889d-10d4-51c4-be9b-87b0c97af70e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6189dc4e-a81c-5882-83eb-6da2f69c3dcc" :answer/id #uuid "6189dc4e-a81c-5882-83eb-6da2f69c3dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bace1e39-b96c-5598-91da-f2e30385e626" :answer/id #uuid "bace1e39-b96c-5598-91da-f2e30385e626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e526436b-9a51-5f65-a668-0eb96ca49eb0" :answer/id #uuid "e526436b-9a51-5f65-a668-0eb96ca49eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198700 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/id #uuid "63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/math-academy-id "q-174455" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\ge -1$\n\nwhere the universal set is $N.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=N.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}\\ge -1$\n\nWe know that the square of any real number is greater than or equal to zero.\n\nSo, the inequality is true for every real number. In particular, it's true for every $x\\in N.$ \n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=N.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/id #uuid "c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" "answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" "answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" "answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" "answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" :answer/id #uuid "2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer/id #uuid "28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" :answer/id #uuid "49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" :answer/id #uuid "2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5" :answer/id #uuid "caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" "question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" "question-29e9adcf-4a5b-51ac-835b-f4a444c16f67"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/id #uuid "9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/math-academy-id "q-175354" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $8$ divided by $t.$\n\nII. $y$ multiplied by $z.$\n\nIII. $p$ is a composite number." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $t$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(y,z)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $p$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" "answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" "answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" "answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" "answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" :answer/id #uuid "e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" :answer/id #uuid "f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" :answer/id #uuid "6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" :answer/id #uuid "e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer/id #uuid "503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/id #uuid "b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/math-academy-id "q-175352" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $q$ plus $3.$\n\nII. $2$ is greater than $x.$\n\nIII. $a$ is a divisor of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $q$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(a,b)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b08c9d99-93d0-59db-a882-7330c0dcbd51"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b08c9d99-93d0-59db-a882-7330c0dcbd51" :answer-field/id #uuid "b08c9d99-93d0-59db-a882-7330c0dcbd51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-397fc5d7-b754-5861-b332-469c54f6a149" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" "answer-7ebde441-31ee-5c72-be00-ba395690a42b" "answer-f4b9e8c0-9717-5691-a9c7-25da739afc28" "answer-397fc5d7-b754-5861-b332-469c54f6a149" "answer-5154ad7e-edfc-5ac5-8a8b-a33d1faff605"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" :answer/id #uuid "9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ebde441-31ee-5c72-be00-ba395690a42b" :answer/id #uuid "7ebde441-31ee-5c72-be00-ba395690a42b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4b9e8c0-9717-5691-a9c7-25da739afc28" :answer/id #uuid "f4b9e8c0-9717-5691-a9c7-25da739afc28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-397fc5d7-b754-5861-b332-469c54f6a149" :answer/id #uuid "397fc5d7-b754-5861-b332-469c54f6a149" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5154ad7e-edfc-5ac5-8a8b-a33d1faff605" :answer/id #uuid "5154ad7e-edfc-5ac5-8a8b-a33d1faff605" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-29e9adcf-4a5b-51ac-835b-f4a444c16f67" :question/id #uuid "29e9adcf-4a5b-51ac-835b-f4a444c16f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-175346" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ is a negative number.\n\nII. $q$ is a multiple of $3.$\n\nIII. $p$ is an irrational number." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $q$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $p$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32567726-3501-5d0d-940f-48d231eb6ef4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32567726-3501-5d0d-940f-48d231eb6ef4" :answer-field/id #uuid "32567726-3501-5d0d-940f-48d231eb6ef4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d537ac14-0b1b-5cb4-8513-cee40f6be506" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e51cc954-0758-54e1-9a16-24656e0a29ea" "answer-73240a1b-211b-5c00-9d5f-311dfb49c53f" "answer-d537ac14-0b1b-5cb4-8513-cee40f6be506" "answer-9eca26cf-f171-5ff3-acfa-60e419b348ec" "answer-2a998714-cd73-5c76-8918-2d96cd4eb205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e51cc954-0758-54e1-9a16-24656e0a29ea" :answer/id #uuid "e51cc954-0758-54e1-9a16-24656e0a29ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73240a1b-211b-5c00-9d5f-311dfb49c53f" :answer/id #uuid "73240a1b-211b-5c00-9d5f-311dfb49c53f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d537ac14-0b1b-5cb4-8513-cee40f6be506" :answer/id #uuid "d537ac14-0b1b-5cb4-8513-cee40f6be506" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9eca26cf-f171-5ff3-acfa-60e419b348ec" :answer/id #uuid "9eca26cf-f171-5ff3-acfa-60e419b348ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a998714-cd73-5c76-8918-2d96cd4eb205" :answer/id #uuid "2a998714-cd73-5c76-8918-2d96cd4eb205" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198281 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" "question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" "question-d193d524-b905-5ac6-8d71-b915f99a8936" "question-11e39500-6de6-5573-ad9b-383cb406fe12"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/id #uuid "ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/math-academy-id "q-174401" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4$\n\nLet's first rearrange our inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{4}<1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that this represents an ellipse centered at $O$ with semi-axes $2$ and $1.$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/fd/fdb0a299dd6ee0bd58ceb1a74c9423bf5cac81857b0538dcda7f0a4cba9a1108.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" "answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" "answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" "answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" "answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" :answer/id #uuid "1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/14/14031d9643e2bb32ad00e8f715e62399b68a970ba56f0aede4d718ad187084d6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" :answer/id #uuid "adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/17/178f6746c8a9984f163b398317da9c5b40fa84331a5643625e63fcb1439c9d0c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" :answer/id #uuid "a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c0/c058c940715b7a2a4a844a360d88cda3daa6455eed159fbee0dfb7545ddbf1a6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer/id #uuid "9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fd/fdb0a299dd6ee0bd58ceb1a74c9423bf5cac81857b0538dcda7f0a4cba9a1108.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17" :answer/id #uuid "c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fe/fef6b4ac68f92490c510e0570968e0f2efbe92de0ec60b1eb4c99545a2713259.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/id #uuid "78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-175387" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $x+y<3,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x+y<3$\n\nNow, we convert the inequality into the slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & <3 \\\\ y & <-x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/bd/bde3d6ee1e58d33088ffc49913e1cd8a299f0ea91cdf4024fd0b63a598ebf456.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0ca923a-2a7a-5fd9-9f3d-f9780ce16762"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0ca923a-2a7a-5fd9-9f3d-f9780ce16762" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ca923a-2a7a-5fd9-9f3d-f9780ce16762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f367dd50-d225-58b4-a8fd-ac8528e6d425" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9452c82b-1bc0-577c-8506-8fd46e8d9124" "answer-fb420cdf-fcbe-56fc-bc90-16106d7638d8" "answer-f367dd50-d225-58b4-a8fd-ac8528e6d425" "answer-5a439630-8d79-5b90-abcd-597163892518" "answer-0b598162-ce03-5219-b00a-ccb35c36a02e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9452c82b-1bc0-577c-8506-8fd46e8d9124" :answer/id #uuid "9452c82b-1bc0-577c-8506-8fd46e8d9124" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1f/1f42ddabaeb4d1feb2f08cf04dfd831deabe8c7b8d22207ad18b0b91f5696d81.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb420cdf-fcbe-56fc-bc90-16106d7638d8" :answer/id #uuid "fb420cdf-fcbe-56fc-bc90-16106d7638d8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/33/335a6ccc2f954c7e8ac32e1eda42e97ebfffe54462facc5b6de68740600ce64b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f367dd50-d225-58b4-a8fd-ac8528e6d425" :answer/id #uuid "f367dd50-d225-58b4-a8fd-ac8528e6d425" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/71/710ef1af1d4b42cc6646272739b70c209222a0a5c7d10aaae039575b5c1040ac.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a439630-8d79-5b90-abcd-597163892518" :answer/id #uuid "5a439630-8d79-5b90-abcd-597163892518" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8d/8dd2a6022bef5b0d739c055d6e5efaac6d17bd54b9d6a8c35eaca5749ac021cf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b598162-ce03-5219-b00a-ccb35c36a02e" :answer/id #uuid "0b598162-ce03-5219-b00a-ccb35c36a02e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b1/b130d69c699465509e862d0e3f4253d0779f25b1e5677308d1e4e0dbaa18cfea.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d193d524-b905-5ac6-8d71-b915f99a8936" :question/id #uuid "d193d524-b905-5ac6-8d71-b915f99a8936" :question/math-academy-id "q-175383" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $a+b$ is an odd number,\n\nwhere the universal set is $\\{(a,b)\\,|\\,a=2,3,\\,b=5,8\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\{2,3\\}\\times \\{5,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{(2,5),(2,8),(3,5),(3,8)\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $(a,b)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $a+b$ is an odd number\n\nThe following pairs give the elements of our truth set:\n\n- $(2,5)$ since $2+5=7$ and $7$ is an odd number,\n\n- $(3,8)$ since $3+8=11$ and $11$ is an odd number.\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=\\{(2,5),(3,8)\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28f10fe3-37fc-540c-8f33-9718dc4bbd85"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28f10fe3-37fc-540c-8f33-9718dc4bbd85" :answer-field/id #uuid "28f10fe3-37fc-540c-8f33-9718dc4bbd85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-efcd6648-fb9e-5966-8e39-df3feb11ef64" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0a0106c-90ba-5cde-b9f6-7d9a1025b6fb" "answer-e101acf5-edd5-58b3-a8a9-fcbb2e84e969" "answer-efcd6648-fb9e-5966-8e39-df3feb11ef64" "answer-753a15d1-3896-52b2-8a66-8e5995eb854b" "answer-c72a41f9-ea14-50d0-8c14-045b9a0abc2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0a0106c-90ba-5cde-b9f6-7d9a1025b6fb" :answer/id #uuid "f0a0106c-90ba-5cde-b9f6-7d9a1025b6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(2,5),(2,8),(3,5),(3,8)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e101acf5-edd5-58b3-a8a9-fcbb2e84e969" :answer/id #uuid "e101acf5-edd5-58b3-a8a9-fcbb2e84e969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(2,5),(3,5),(3,8)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efcd6648-fb9e-5966-8e39-df3feb11ef64" :answer/id #uuid "efcd6648-fb9e-5966-8e39-df3feb11ef64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(2,5),(3,8)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-753a15d1-3896-52b2-8a66-8e5995eb854b" :answer/id #uuid "753a15d1-3896-52b2-8a66-8e5995eb854b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(2,8),(3,5)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c72a41f9-ea14-50d0-8c14-045b9a0abc2a" :answer/id #uuid "c72a41f9-ea14-50d0-8c14-045b9a0abc2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-11e39500-6de6-5573-ad9b-383cb406fe12" :question/id #uuid "11e39500-6de6-5573-ad9b-383cb406fe12" :question/math-academy-id "q-175389" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $-x+y\\ge -1,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $-x+y\\ge -1$\n\nNow, we convert the inequality into the slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+y & \\ge -1 \\\\ y & \\ge x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/8d/8dabb7d13ef6e46cc31a2613bf7d62a5163db96630e9a855e84b9335e3be4855.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e425688d-cefc-532f-960d-cb1285b1d995"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e425688d-cefc-532f-960d-cb1285b1d995" :answer-field/id #uuid "e425688d-cefc-532f-960d-cb1285b1d995" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-62fc9842-761e-5620-a946-dfc980712891" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62fc9842-761e-5620-a946-dfc980712891" "answer-878fcaba-04c3-596f-b953-6f9266034438" "answer-f88622e3-3f4a-580d-a704-ac22eb4e1cc2" "answer-d5581895-7cdd-5211-b6e9-266caf79785b" "answer-3b9d16c0-f580-537f-9b8f-77b2a081c034"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62fc9842-761e-5620-a946-dfc980712891" :answer/id #uuid "62fc9842-761e-5620-a946-dfc980712891" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2f/2f1b90e7143a3829d90ec3d9ea7c5378740f9e60a3715725f2b96a850e2037cd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-878fcaba-04c3-596f-b953-6f9266034438" :answer/id #uuid "878fcaba-04c3-596f-b953-6f9266034438" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/38/382ebe19c2b0a4dc6d8c4c7c2266dbcf02bdd0e8311c627cf79bee1eb75e5126.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f88622e3-3f4a-580d-a704-ac22eb4e1cc2" :answer/id #uuid "f88622e3-3f4a-580d-a704-ac22eb4e1cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/57/57b5404aacae6482ee69c5e00034c30d4f0a7a9ec237c8961a2bfa7babcb6042.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5581895-7cdd-5211-b6e9-266caf79785b" :answer/id #uuid "d5581895-7cdd-5211-b6e9-266caf79785b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/6d/6d2647e04beb52c1faaebfb234114a231ffe1c8e6ef3304e1b54787b3d363c8f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b9d16c0-f580-537f-9b8f-77b2a081c034" :answer/id #uuid "3b9d16c0-f580-537f-9b8f-77b2a081c034" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cf/cf7e26d20291c340dd701aee6d2c9d38c0f83059262ffc8a1408b9ac0342e762.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f74663e2-eda6-5c43-8b1e-ec79f6eff3d7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f74663e2-eda6-5c43-8b1e-ec79f6eff3d7" :question/id #uuid "f74663e2-eda6-5c43-8b1e-ec79f6eff3d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129445" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2$ at the point $(1,2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2) & =3({1}^{2})({2}^{2})=12 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) & =2({1}^{3})(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-2 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) \\\\ z-2 & =12(x-1)+4(y-2) \\\\ z-2 & =12x+4y-20 \\\\ 12x+4y-z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e280a27-9de7-5a03-bfcc-a35615144270"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e280a27-9de7-5a03-bfcc-a35615144270" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e280a27-9de7-5a03-bfcc-a35615144270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ab27aa7-e26f-5b28-a61b-7d75dd7e76a0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ab27aa7-e26f-5b28-a61b-7d75dd7e76a0" "answer-50e0bc24-5e3a-552f-97d8-44ee57ea98a0" "answer-7a0a3654-4f3f-52be-a0f9-b305d2f93119" "answer-c4d8dbf8-7fb7-5f92-a1ba-286efca1292a" "answer-ec6a76ae-df6b-5fc7-8f39-9ed699a44710"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab27aa7-e26f-5b28-a61b-7d75dd7e76a0" :answer/id #uuid "0ab27aa7-e26f-5b28-a61b-7d75dd7e76a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12x+4y-z-18=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50e0bc24-5e3a-552f-97d8-44ee57ea98a0" :answer/id #uuid "50e0bc24-5e3a-552f-97d8-44ee57ea98a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12x-4y+z-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a0a3654-4f3f-52be-a0f9-b305d2f93119" :answer/id #uuid "7a0a3654-4f3f-52be-a0f9-b305d2f93119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+2y+z-12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4d8dbf8-7fb7-5f92-a1ba-286efca1292a" :answer/id #uuid "c4d8dbf8-7fb7-5f92-a1ba-286efca1292a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-4y+z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec6a76ae-df6b-5fc7-8f39-9ed699a44710" :answer/id #uuid "ec6a76ae-df6b-5fc7-8f39-9ed699a44710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x-y+z-8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129613 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6f62591f-ce02-5d1d-a041-40b4fa4f0093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6f62591f-ce02-5d1d-a041-40b4fa4f0093" :question/id #uuid "6f62591f-ce02-5d1d-a041-40b4fa4f0093" :question/math-academy-id "q-129487" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0,2,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=-2y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,2) & =2(1)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,2) & =-2(0)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,2) & =2(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,2)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,2)+(z-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,2) \\\\ w-5 & =2(x-1)+0y+4(z-2) \\\\ w-5 & =2x+4z-10 \\\\ 2x+4z-w-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d53eb4df-306d-5fe9-a04a-ef268bb57a12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d53eb4df-306d-5fe9-a04a-ef268bb57a12" :answer-field/id #uuid "d53eb4df-306d-5fe9-a04a-ef268bb57a12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0d46eb51-fbd4-5527-a391-ea1f1472e1f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d46eb51-fbd4-5527-a391-ea1f1472e1f5" "answer-65d02bda-6ee0-5093-a005-04eff527cec0" "answer-07f2d355-8b47-5410-897b-016de7e6340d" "answer-6ca0d6d0-706e-5535-9a5c-90b235616840" "answer-e6c72a8e-2ca4-5b18-9f33-e6a6209fea4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d46eb51-fbd4-5527-a391-ea1f1472e1f5" :answer/id #uuid "0d46eb51-fbd4-5527-a391-ea1f1472e1f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+4z-w-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65d02bda-6ee0-5093-a005-04eff527cec0" :answer/id #uuid "65d02bda-6ee0-5093-a005-04eff527cec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3z-w-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07f2d355-8b47-5410-897b-016de7e6340d" :answer/id #uuid "07f2d355-8b47-5410-897b-016de7e6340d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca0d6d0-706e-5535-9a5c-90b235616840" :answer/id #uuid "6ca0d6d0-706e-5535-9a5c-90b235616840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+2z-w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c72a8e-2ca4-5b18-9f33-e6a6209fea4f" :answer/id #uuid "e6c72a8e-2ca4-5b18-9f33-e6a6209fea4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4y+w-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6c4bc11a-cdaa-550d-94a0-3ff2e50cf498" "question-8f164f90-e76a-54c1-a336-782b45d61bdf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c4bc11a-cdaa-550d-94a0-3ff2e50cf498" :question/id #uuid "6c4bc11a-cdaa-550d-94a0-3ff2e50cf498" :question/math-academy-id "q-15103" :question/problem "Suppose that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{6}$ is the sixth partial sum of $S.$ According to the alternating series error bound, $|S-{s}_{6}|<k$ for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}}{{n}^{2}}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $6$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{6}|<|{b}_{7}|=|\\frac{(-1)^{7}}{{7}^{2}}|=\\frac{1}{49}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{1}{49}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a59751e-949f-5d36-80c1-fa6f0759ee0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a59751e-949f-5d36-80c1-fa6f0759ee0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a59751e-949f-5d36-80c1-fa6f0759ee0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f26e9ff2-3fea-5e99-8496-28dd0c86a06d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19048534-c446-541b-92e4-f87a572f0445" "answer-f26e9ff2-3fea-5e99-8496-28dd0c86a06d" "answer-2986023f-c3b0-5d34-89e7-d5b18cc1b181" "answer-660039ee-808b-5909-a6a4-855d47eca687" "answer-c054db7d-8b25-59ff-85a1-fc53976cbd21"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19048534-c446-541b-92e4-f87a572f0445" :answer/id #uuid "19048534-c446-541b-92e4-f87a572f0445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f26e9ff2-3fea-5e99-8496-28dd0c86a06d" :answer/id #uuid "f26e9ff2-3fea-5e99-8496-28dd0c86a06d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{49}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2986023f-c3b0-5d34-89e7-d5b18cc1b181" :answer/id #uuid "2986023f-c3b0-5d34-89e7-d5b18cc1b181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-660039ee-808b-5909-a6a4-855d47eca687" :answer/id #uuid "660039ee-808b-5909-a6a4-855d47eca687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{49}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c054db7d-8b25-59ff-85a1-fc53976cbd21" :answer/id #uuid "c054db7d-8b25-59ff-85a1-fc53976cbd21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{49}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f164f90-e76a-54c1-a336-782b45d61bdf" :question/id #uuid "8f164f90-e76a-54c1-a336-782b45d61bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-352756" :question/problem "Suppose that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}\\,n!}{(n+4)!}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{6}$ is the sixth partial sum of $S.$ According to the alternating series error bound, $|S-{s}_{6}|<k$ for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{n!}{(n+4)!}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}\\,n!}{(n+4)!}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $6$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{6}|<|{b}_{7}|=|\\frac{{(-1)}^{7}\\,7!}{(7+4)!}|=\\frac{7!}{11!}=\\frac{1}{8\\cdot 9\\cdot 10\\cdot 11}=\\frac{1}{7920}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{1}{7920}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-159b45da-df98-533e-a437-a9180419cd3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-159b45da-df98-533e-a437-a9180419cd3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "159b45da-df98-533e-a437-a9180419cd3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cc145cd2-9498-5331-8842-8de1cc06800b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc145cd2-9498-5331-8842-8de1cc06800b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc145cd2-9498-5331-8842-8de1cc06800b" :answer/id #uuid "cc145cd2-9498-5331-8842-8de1cc06800b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7920}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b6f1577d-5608-56ec-bbab-86d743866f2e" "question-fd9b72de-d1e8-5e4c-b443-057fdab0329d" "question-8f270d15-6fe5-55df-829e-27dd74957fdc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6f1577d-5608-56ec-bbab-86d743866f2e" :question/id #uuid "b6f1577d-5608-56ec-bbab-86d743866f2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-352762" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{n({n}^{2}+4)}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{i}$ is the $i$th partial sum of $S,$ use the alternating series error bound to determine an inequality that gives the values of $i$ such that\n$|S-{s}_{i}|<0.05.$\n\n${i}^{3}+3{i}^{2}+7i+5\\ge$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{n({n}^{2}+4)}\\,\\text{and}\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{n({n}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nThen ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 2$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause the series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nThus, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{b}_{i+1}|=|\\frac{3(-1)^{i+2}}{(i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4)}| & \\le 0.05 \\\\ \\frac{3}{(i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4)} & \\le \\frac{1}{20} \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4) \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)({i}^{2}+2i+1+4) \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)({i}^{2}+2i+5) \\\\ 60 & \\le {i}^{3}+3{i}^{2}+7i+5 \\\\ {i}^{3}+3{i}^{2}+7i+5 & \\ge 60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdd473d7-ac4e-56be-8ce8-60ffb0f1e888"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdd473d7-ac4e-56be-8ce8-60ffb0f1e888" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd473d7-ac4e-56be-8ce8-60ffb0f1e888" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6fbc8956-7af9-5d82-88ed-b5cd5cfd7c9c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fbc8956-7af9-5d82-88ed-b5cd5cfd7c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fbc8956-7af9-5d82-88ed-b5cd5cfd7c9c" :answer/id #uuid "6fbc8956-7af9-5d82-88ed-b5cd5cfd7c9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd9b72de-d1e8-5e4c-b443-057fdab0329d" :question/id #uuid "fd9b72de-d1e8-5e4c-b443-057fdab0329d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352763" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-1)}^{n+1}}{\\sqrt{n+1}}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{i}$ is the $i$th partial sum of $S,$ use the alternating series error bound to determine the values of $i$ such that $|S-{s}_{i}|<0.01.$\n\n$i\\ge$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n+1}}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{\\sqrt{n+1}}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 1$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test. \n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nSo, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{(-1)^{i+2}}{\\sqrt{(i+1)+1}}| & \\le 0.01 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{i+2}} & \\le \\frac{1}{100} \\\\ \\sqrt[2]{i+2} & \\ge 100 \\\\ (i+2)^{1/2} & \\ge 100 \\\\ i+2 & \\ge (100)^{2} \\\\ i+2 & \\ge 10000 \\\\ i & \\ge 9998.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bf1afec-fd1f-50cb-988c-1d344a155a6e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bf1afec-fd1f-50cb-988c-1d344a155a6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf1afec-fd1f-50cb-988c-1d344a155a6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b170842b-5b2d-5078-a5a6-acb218dd45e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b170842b-5b2d-5078-a5a6-acb218dd45e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b170842b-5b2d-5078-a5a6-acb218dd45e4" :answer/id #uuid "b170842b-5b2d-5078-a5a6-acb218dd45e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9998" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f270d15-6fe5-55df-829e-27dd74957fdc" :question/id #uuid "8f270d15-6fe5-55df-829e-27dd74957fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-352774" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=3}^{\\infty }\\frac{{2(-1)}^{n}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2n+1)}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{i}$ is the $i$th partial sum of $S,$ use the alternating series error bound to determine an inequality that gives the values of $i$ such that $|S-{s}_{i}|<0.2.$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2i+3)\\ge$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2n+1)}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}\\,2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2n+1)}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 3$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test. \n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nSo, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{b}_{i+1}|=|\\frac{(-1)^{i+1}\\,2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2(i+1)+1)}| & \\le 0.2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2i+3)} & \\le 0.2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2i+3)} & \\le \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 10 & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2i+3) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2i+3) & \\ge 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3de1ab9d-bf97-57ce-8fb8-7959134261a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3de1ab9d-bf97-57ce-8fb8-7959134261a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "3de1ab9d-bf97-57ce-8fb8-7959134261a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ccf8156a-5145-53a0-acb6-e6e427f7cdcf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccf8156a-5145-53a0-acb6-e6e427f7cdcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccf8156a-5145-53a0-acb6-e6e427f7cdcf" :answer/id #uuid "ccf8156a-5145-53a0-acb6-e6e427f7cdcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9a0c4459-7e42-515e-ba77-ca28d96e8d50" :activity/id #uuid "9a0c4459-7e42-515e-ba77-ca28d96e8d50" :activity/title "The Alternating Series Error Bound" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050912 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-50136f0e-287a-5a86-9add-5cd78eb80231" "step-d8a5ca47-6ee4-5751-a8ec-ed05ca31f3fd" "step-53829707-e1e6-5a85-8f73-c25dca5844f9" "step-882b7db4-09fc-5e93-b1f6-eb88c65a7948" "step-212a1ba6-0439-5eb5-9fa6-0549590c783c"] :activity/first-step "step-50136f0e-287a-5a86-9add-5cd78eb80231" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-50136f0e-287a-5a86-9add-5cd78eb80231" :step/id #uuid "50136f0e-287a-5a86-9add-5cd78eb80231" :step/content "question-6c4bc11a-cdaa-550d-94a0-3ff2e50cf498" :step/next "step-d8a5ca47-6ee4-5751-a8ec-ed05ca31f3fd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d8a5ca47-6ee4-5751-a8ec-ed05ca31f3fd" :step/id #uuid "d8a5ca47-6ee4-5751-a8ec-ed05ca31f3fd" :step/content "question-8f164f90-e76a-54c1-a336-782b45d61bdf" :step/next "step-53829707-e1e6-5a85-8f73-c25dca5844f9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-53829707-e1e6-5a85-8f73-c25dca5844f9" :step/id #uuid "53829707-e1e6-5a85-8f73-c25dca5844f9" :step/content "question-b6f1577d-5608-56ec-bbab-86d743866f2e" :step/next "step-882b7db4-09fc-5e93-b1f6-eb88c65a7948" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-882b7db4-09fc-5e93-b1f6-eb88c65a7948" :step/id #uuid "882b7db4-09fc-5e93-b1f6-eb88c65a7948" :step/content "question-fd9b72de-d1e8-5e4c-b443-057fdab0329d" :step/next "step-212a1ba6-0439-5eb5-9fa6-0549590c783c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-212a1ba6-0439-5eb5-9fa6-0549590c783c" :step/id #uuid "212a1ba6-0439-5eb5-9fa6-0549590c783c" :step/content "question-8f270d15-6fe5-55df-829e-27dd74957fdc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083322 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579" :question/id #uuid "543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579" :question/math-academy-id "q-9787" :question/problem "The owner of a restaurant noted that $145$ vegetarian customers visited his restaurant during a particular week. On a particular day of the same week, he noted that $x=15$ vegetarian customers visited the restaurant, corresponding to a $z$-score of $z=-1.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the number of vegetarian customers per day, giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the mean number of vegetarian customers for each day:\n\n$$\n\\overset{¯}{x}=\\frac{145}{7}=20.71\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places.\n\nThe $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set. Rewriting this in terms of $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{z}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard deviation $\\sigma$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\frac{x-\\overset{¯}{x}}{z} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-20.71}{-1.5} \\\\  & =3.81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ad868d2-4b59-59e5-af41-cdcaa965a99b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc6c033b-6092-5094-8efd-03c857a491a2" "answer-d87a2113-3ca9-5e90-9173-5ef22a26472f" "answer-b75010ed-05a2-5fae-94e7-e38cb062d94a" "answer-526b6aa7-3f19-53ef-a532-7f9286139f53" "answer-3ad868d2-4b59-59e5-af41-cdcaa965a99b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc6c033b-6092-5094-8efd-03c857a491a2" :answer/id #uuid "dc6c033b-6092-5094-8efd-03c857a491a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d87a2113-3ca9-5e90-9173-5ef22a26472f" :answer/id #uuid "d87a2113-3ca9-5e90-9173-5ef22a26472f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b75010ed-05a2-5fae-94e7-e38cb062d94a" :answer/id #uuid "b75010ed-05a2-5fae-94e7-e38cb062d94a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-526b6aa7-3f19-53ef-a532-7f9286139f53" :answer/id #uuid "526b6aa7-3f19-53ef-a532-7f9286139f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ad868d2-4b59-59e5-af41-cdcaa965a99b" :answer/id #uuid "3ad868d2-4b59-59e5-af41-cdcaa965a99b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083227 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af87d523-ac60-5aec-8cf6-a5f255a961ed" "question-50d225de-7004-5810-a19e-8625e7e461c1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af87d523-ac60-5aec-8cf6-a5f255a961ed" :question/id #uuid "af87d523-ac60-5aec-8cf6-a5f255a961ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-94473" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=16$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =2.5.$ Find the value of an observation that has $z$-score $z=-0.4.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{¯}{x}=16,$ $z=-0.4,$ and $\\sigma =2.5$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\  & =16+(-0.4)\\cdot 2.5 \\\\  & =16-1 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3433b4b-8883-5522-b986-cd5716b0db79"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3433b4b-8883-5522-b986-cd5716b0db79" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3433b4b-8883-5522-b986-cd5716b0db79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c3652fcb-627b-5e2d-87c4-3c8135bc864b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8b2b3cc-8ebe-5843-8f10-433a90a3310c" "answer-ae404e3a-dbf6-5282-b23e-6e487d6722fb" "answer-9a53cb31-bc17-5daf-8994-cbb6560d170a" "answer-c3652fcb-627b-5e2d-87c4-3c8135bc864b" "answer-d0d16dea-91d4-5e65-88b9-96458855ddc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8b2b3cc-8ebe-5843-8f10-433a90a3310c" :answer/id #uuid "e8b2b3cc-8ebe-5843-8f10-433a90a3310c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae404e3a-dbf6-5282-b23e-6e487d6722fb" :answer/id #uuid "ae404e3a-dbf6-5282-b23e-6e487d6722fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a53cb31-bc17-5daf-8994-cbb6560d170a" :answer/id #uuid "9a53cb31-bc17-5daf-8994-cbb6560d170a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3652fcb-627b-5e2d-87c4-3c8135bc864b" :answer/id #uuid "c3652fcb-627b-5e2d-87c4-3c8135bc864b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0d16dea-91d4-5e65-88b9-96458855ddc7" :answer/id #uuid "d0d16dea-91d4-5e65-88b9-96458855ddc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-50d225de-7004-5810-a19e-8625e7e461c1" :question/id #uuid "50d225de-7004-5810-a19e-8625e7e461c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-332028" :question/problem "A data set has a standard deviation $\\sigma =2.4$ and an unknown mean. An observation of the data set has the value $x=5.4$ and $z$-score $z=0.5.$ Find the mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{―}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5.4,$ $z=0.5,$ and $\\sigma =2.4$ into the formula and solving for $\\overset{―}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}+0.5\\cdot 2.4 \\\\ 5.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}+1.2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =4.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1c5c354f-b3fb-557e-b2a1-3bac47f270b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1c5c354f-b3fb-557e-b2a1-3bac47f270b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c5c354f-b3fb-557e-b2a1-3bac47f270b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6137d563-5854-54cb-a38e-1055473864b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6137d563-5854-54cb-a38e-1055473864b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6137d563-5854-54cb-a38e-1055473864b8" :answer/id #uuid "6137d563-5854-54cb-a38e-1055473864b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083323 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e17b593f-806a-5407-8b55-7558d69aa888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e17b593f-806a-5407-8b55-7558d69aa888" :question/id #uuid "e17b593f-806a-5407-8b55-7558d69aa888" :question/math-academy-id "q-332244" :question/problem "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=3.1,{x}_{2}=7.9$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-0.5$ and ${z}_{2}=1.5,$ respectively. Find the standard deviation $\\sigma$ of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma\n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n3.1=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-0.5)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n7.9=\\overset{¯}{x}+1.5\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.9-3.1 & =(1.5-(-0.5))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 4.8 & =2\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-332a9a32-3521-5a06-a046-98035661faf9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-332a9a32-3521-5a06-a046-98035661faf9" :answer-field/id #uuid "332a9a32-3521-5a06-a046-98035661faf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6d31a8c1-021c-5a4c-876f-09f1568ff61b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6d31a8c1-021c-5a4c-876f-09f1568ff61b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d31a8c1-021c-5a4c-876f-09f1568ff61b" :answer/id #uuid "6d31a8c1-021c-5a4c-876f-09f1568ff61b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-81f06c37-0e57-589d-ba7c-883c5c4cad26" :activity/id #uuid "81f06c37-0e57-589d-ba7c-883c5c4cad26" :