that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$5.60$ per foot, to find the price per yard, we multiply by $3:$\n\n$$\n5.60\\times 3=16.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gold wire costs $\\$16.80$ per yard." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc1a6bc1-e6b7-5531-84ae-b676cb38f400"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc1a6bc1-e6b7-5531-84ae-b676cb38f400" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1a6bc1-e6b7-5531-84ae-b676cb38f400" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-826c5023-ef86-5ab9-acaa-ec789d00fac6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7abd7d8f-b5de-5cfc-b3bf-1a23c149a745" "answer-a0bb0036-fab5-5d80-ba7d-7ad30685b95d" "answer-51be7f7b-234a-535f-8314-06a596ba3268" "answer-826c5023-ef86-5ab9-acaa-ec789d00fac6" "answer-9d87d5ae-077e-5462-9e51-8ecda822620f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7abd7d8f-b5de-5cfc-b3bf-1a23c149a745" :answer/id #uuid "7abd7d8f-b5de-5cfc-b3bf-1a23c149a745" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$12.25$ per yard" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0bb0036-fab5-5d80-ba7d-7ad30685b95d" :answer/id #uuid "a0bb0036-fab5-5d80-ba7d-7ad30685b95d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$14.75$ per yard" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51be7f7b-234a-535f-8314-06a596ba3268" :answer/id #uuid "51be7f7b-234a-535f-8314-06a596ba3268" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$15.60$ per yard" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-826c5023-ef86-5ab9-acaa-ec789d00fac6" :answer/id #uuid "826c5023-ef86-5ab9-acaa-ec789d00fac6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$16.80$ per yard" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d87d5ae-077e-5462-9e51-8ecda822620f" :answer/id #uuid "9d87d5ae-077e-5462-9e51-8ecda822620f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$18.20$ per yard" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3c42dde-368f-51a4-a96b-0c5d0e222f8f" :question/id #uuid "e3c42dde-368f-51a4-a96b-0c5d0e222f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-354923" :question/problem "A scientist bought $1$ fluid ounce of a chemical solution and paid $\\$1.60$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that there are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$1.60$ per fluid ounce, to find the price per cup, we multiply by $8:$\n\n$$\n1.60\\times 8=12.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the chemical solution costs $\\$12.80$ per cup." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44ddfc6b-4838-5599-a86f-bf8221237272"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44ddfc6b-4838-5599-a86f-bf8221237272" :answer-field/id #uuid "44ddfc6b-4838-5599-a86f-bf8221237272" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3497fac9-fc4e-56a7-bdbf-3df6bb29d82a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b0c9344-df9c-5f3f-b871-4631ff371574" "answer-3497fac9-fc4e-56a7-bdbf-3df6bb29d82a" "answer-d62a7cd4-5580-5f49-81c7-8e925474945a" "answer-2be12b11-3652-52e4-adce-89e1e7625e58" "answer-2ed0b6cc-dc15-5ab5-8bc7-84da3585b4ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b0c9344-df9c-5f3f-b871-4631ff371574" :answer/id #uuid "5b0c9344-df9c-5f3f-b871-4631ff371574" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$10.20$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3497fac9-fc4e-56a7-bdbf-3df6bb29d82a" :answer/id #uuid "3497fac9-fc4e-56a7-bdbf-3df6bb29d82a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$12.80$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d62a7cd4-5580-5f49-81c7-8e925474945a" :answer/id #uuid "d62a7cd4-5580-5f49-81c7-8e925474945a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$14.40$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2be12b11-3652-52e4-adce-89e1e7625e58" :answer/id #uuid "2be12b11-3652-52e4-adce-89e1e7625e58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$8.00$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ed0b6cc-dc15-5ab5-8bc7-84da3585b4ac" :answer/id #uuid "2ed0b6cc-dc15-5ab5-8bc7-84da3585b4ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$9.60$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b574a7a-bdad-59b8-aadb-22d876ef5c0b" :question/id #uuid "4b574a7a-bdad-59b8-aadb-22d876ef5c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-354928" :question/problem "Emily filled a container with $48$ fluid ounces of juice and paid $\\$11.52$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$     \n\n$$\n48÷8=6\n$$\n\nSo, $48$ fluid ounces is the same as $6$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $6:$ \n\n$$\n11.52÷6=1.92\n$$\n\nTherefore, the juice costs $\\$1.92$ per cup." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffbd78f3-a124-58f1-9f81-8177785c5280"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffbd78f3-a124-58f1-9f81-8177785c5280" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffbd78f3-a124-58f1-9f81-8177785c5280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-210351d0-1105-53ce-b4c8-02147d3c6fd7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09f9eee1-0098-5229-b9ce-e4b65237d12f" "answer-747d7d4b-1fd2-5d3e-86b4-da9429862057" "answer-210351d0-1105-53ce-b4c8-02147d3c6fd7" "answer-42e3a724-292a-58b1-ac69-9a6cb1767985" "answer-1e0f4944-55fa-5715-8483-aaea1dc8f44d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09f9eee1-0098-5229-b9ce-e4b65237d12f" :answer/id #uuid "09f9eee1-0098-5229-b9ce-e4b65237d12f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\$0.24$ per cup" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-747d7d